{"id": "g2_sum_abs_distinct_nonzero_mult9", "signature": "solve(values)", "statement": "Given a list of integers `values`, consider the DISTINCT values that are nonzero multiples of 9 (negative multiples count; zero does not). Return the sum of the absolute values of those distinct values. Repeated values count once, but -9 and 9 are two different values, so both contribute 9 to the sum. Return 0 if there are none, including for an empty list.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[9]], "expected": 9}, {"args": [[-9]], "expected": 9}, {"args": [[9, -9]], "expected": 18}, {"args": [[9, 9, 9]], "expected": 9}, {"args": [[0]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[0, 18, -18, 27]], "expected": 63}, {"args": [[1, 2, 3]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[45, -45, 45, 5]], "expected": 90}, {"args": [[90, -180, 8]], "expected": 270}, {"args": [[-27, -27, 27, 36]], "expected": 90}, {"args": [[7, 11, 13]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[-9, -9, 0, 9, 9]], "expected": 18}], "facts": [["arg", "values", "int_list"], ["iterate", "values"], ["remainder", "9", "0"], ["drop", "zero"], ["map", "abs"], ["distinct", "original"], ["aggregate", "sum"], ["size", "values", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["seq_fold"], "uses": [], "solution_sha256": "b4810eed778bdb9d08fad4cda37d8dc742d6c4df4b6eda23bf1ff27740a470e4", "reference_sha256": "5dde36dd1afe8033b8c68ae8ede159fb25a737863be5ac265d035f4620b490cf"}}